Ten more REST endpoints are now exposed as MCP tools (constructs, files, folders/templates listing metadata, languages, markup languages, object properties, part types, publish protocol log, maintenance status and page rendering), covering a wider range of argument shapes: multiple parameter beans combined in a single tool, method parameters annotated directly with @com.gentics.contentnode.rest.mcp.McpToolParam@ instead of only bean fields, @List@/@Set@ collections, and enums.

To support this, @com.gentics.contentnode.mcp.McpToolRegistry@ was hardened in two ways: it now rejects a tool whose input schema would combine two parameters/fields into the same argument name, instead of one silently overwriting the other; and its check for JAX-RS @@Context@ injection is now per-method rather than per-class - a static bytecode analysis (via a new @com.gentics.contentnode.mcp.ContextUsageAnalyzer@) determines whether a tool method (or a method it calls within its own class hierarchy) actually reads a @@Context@ field, so a method that happens to live on a class with such a field, but doesn't touch it, is no longer blocked from registration.
